From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:35:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: ignore non-WED TX rate on MT7990

With WED active, ordinary data packets use MT_PACKET_ID_WED.  A TX status
with MT_PACKET_ID_NO_SKB can instead describe a fixed-rate control frame.
On MT7990 such a sparse status was observed replacing the station's cached
HE80 payload rate with legacy OFDM 6 Mbit/s while the firmware continued to
report HE80 MCS11.

mt76 passes the cached rate back to mac80211 with subsequent TX
completions.  mac80211 then uses it to estimate pending airtime for AQL.
Treating the control-frame rate as the payload rate can make AQL throttle
the queue to about 90 Mbit/s.  The common connac2 TX-status path already
avoids this by caching only MT_PACKET_ID_WED rates when WED is in use.

Apply the same rule narrowly to MT7990 while WED is active.  Keep the
current behavior for MT7996, MT7992, and MT7990 without WED.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/issues/1043
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/mac.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

Index: mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/mt7996/mac.c
===================================================================
--- mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791.orig/mt7996/mac.c
+++ mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1614,7 +1614,9 @@ mt7996_mac_add_txs_skb(struct mt7996_dev
 		stats->tx_bw[0]++;
 		break;
 	}
-	wcid->rate = rate;
+	if (!is_mt7990(mdev) || !mtk_wed_device_active(&mdev->mmio.wed) ||
+	    pid == MT_PACKET_ID_WED)
+		wcid->rate = rate;
 
 out:
 	if (skb)
